  "question": {
    "text": "In a certain region static electric and magnetic fields exist. The magnetic field is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>. If a test charge moving with a velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math> experiences no force in that region, then the electric field in the region, in SI units, is:",
